==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/kʰrauː/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|auː}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|is|non|krá}}, {{m|non|kró}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*kranhō}}, of uncertain origin, found only in {{der|is|gmq}}; possibly related to {{m|gem-pro|*kringaną||to turn}}.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|f|krár|krár}}

# [[pub]]
# a quiet [[corner]], [[nook]]

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-noun-f-s1|kr|á}}

===Etymology 2===
Ultimately from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*krēaną||to crow}}.  Cognate with {{cog|fo|krá}}. Related to English {{m|en|crow}} (noun and verb).

====Interjection====
{{head|is|interjection}}

# {{lb|is|onomatopoeia}} [[caw]] (representing the sound of a raven or crow)

